window.EN={"1":"Breaking through the border, Leif's \"Liberation Army\" has at last advanced into imperial territory.","2":"But an imperial fortress that boasts of being impregnable stands in their way.","3":"Unless they get past this \"Fort Dandrum,\" the road to Tahra will not open...","4":"So, as I have said many times, an enemy has appeared at Fort Noel.","5":"If we don't send reinforcements at once, General Largo is in danger!","6":"Please, General Kempf! Permit my corps to sortie!","7":"You say an enemy has appeared, but who exactly are they?","8":"What is your duty? Scouting, is it not?","9":"You come sauntering back without even grasping that much, and then tell me to send out troops? What is the meaning of that?","10":"The situation was pressing. Every moment counts! That is why I came back to report first.","11":"But if this \"enemy\" you speak of is a decoy to lure us out, what then?","12":"This Fort Dandrum is called impregnable precisely because my 12th Corps is here.","13":"As if I could move troops lightly without even knowing the enemy's true state.","14":"Then what becomes of General Largo! Even as we speak, General Largo is in danger...","15":"One or two old men like that are no great matter to our army.","16":"Left alone he'll drop dead sooner or later. It saves us the trouble.","17":"H-how can you say such a thing... General Kempf!! And you call yourself...","18":"What is that look? Are you saying you'll rebel against me?","19":"Interesting. You surely know what happens if you rebel against a superior officer.","20":"Can you still rebel against me, eh?","21":"Kh...","22":"What's wrong? You talk big, but in the end you can't do anything?","23":"......","24":"Well, you're a naive young lady fresh out of the officers' academy.","25":"About all you can do is go crying to your beloved big brother Reinhardt.","26":"What! What did you just say!","27":"Hm? Didn't you hear?","28":"I said, about all you can do is go crying to your beloved big brother Reinhardt.","29":"...Why, you...","30":"That's right, he'd be sweet to you. After all, seducing women is that man's specialty. Wahahaha.","31":"You dare insult my brother! I won't forgive it!","32":"Oh, you've drawn your sword? And what now, kill me? Heh, you fool.","33":"Guards! Throw General Olwen in prison. Insubordination toward a superior officer, and the crime of rebellion!","34":"Sir!","35":"General Olwen, please come with us.","36":"Kh... General Kempf... how despicable...","37":"Heh. That takes care of that impertinent girl.","38":"If his sister is executed for rebellion, Reinhardt will lose his standing. I can't wait to see his face. Heh heh heh.","39":"General Kempf! What on earth is the meaning of this!","40":"Hm? What's the matter, Fred? You've gone so pale. Did something happen?","41":"Don't play dumb. What exactly are you saying Lady Olwen did?","42":"Humiliating a subordinate over a private grudge is against military law.","43":"Release her from prison at once. Otherwise, I will report this to Princess Ishtar!","44":"\"Private\"? I can't let that pass. General Olwen drew her sword right here. Trying to kill me, her superior.","45":"What!? Surely not... such a thing...","46":"Under military law, what did turning one's sword on a superior officer mean again?","47":"I seem to recall it was a grave crime deserving of death...","48":"...So that was your aim... How cowardly...","49":"Well, that aside, shall I have you take responsibility as adjutant to the traitor Olwen?","50":"I order you to sortie. However, this is a sortie as punishment.","51":"No retreat is allowed; fight until you die. If you slack off, I execute Olwen immediately. Understood!","52":"Kempf!... You shameless wretch!!","53":"Hm? Did you say something? I can't hear you. Wahahahaha...","54":"What! The enemy is flying the flag of Leonster!?","55":"And on top of that, you say the commander is a boy of fourteen or fifteen!","56":"Hmm... That is probably Prince Leif.","57":"Heh, interesting. This may be a chance to win some glory.","58":"All right, I have a plan. Lure them into the east corridor. Operation name: \"Port Chris.\"","59":"Whatever you do, don't let the enemy see through it!","60":"That was quite splendidly done. At this speed, the enemy will have had no chance to escape.","61":"But we must not rest our hands. Most likely, children are being held in this fortress as well.","62":"Let us clear the entire castle and rescue the children as soon as possible!","63":"It took a little time, but to avoid losing soldiers, it could not be helped.","64":"This fort no longer has any strategic value.","65":"Leave the enemy who fled, and for now let us head to the rescue of Tahra as quickly as possible!","66":"Paladin of Friege, is this how you people do things?","67":"When we fought at Noel Canyon, I was impressed, thinking this is the honor-loving Friege army indeed,","68":"but it seems I was mistaken.","69":"For the honor of my duchy, let me say this: a battle like this is not something the Crusader Thrud would recognize.","70":"It all came from that man... from General Kempf's foolishness.","71":"I do not shrink from dying as a knight, but I cannot bear it done this way.","72":"...If you have no will to fight, we will not lay a hand on you.","73":"Not that either of us should have the strength to spare.","74":"True. I, too, still have something left to do.","75":"Very well... Let us each think only of getting out.","76":"Understood. We will try to break into the castle; you should escape to the south.","77":"We'll do something about the door.","78":"It seems I owe you one... I am Fred, a knight of House Schutze. Your name?","79":"...Leif, of the Kingdom of Leonster.","80":"Of Leonster? ...I see... so that's how it is... Then, Sir Leif, we shall meet again someday!","81":"Heh heh heh. He fell for it. The fool.","82":"All right, do it!","83":"Absurd! You mean to fight in a situation like this!!","84":"Olwen... I meant to get you out... Forgive me...","85":"Tch... To think the invincible Dandrum would be breached...","86":"Urgh... How can this be... It can't be helped. We withdraw for now!"};
